WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.900
AI is the most transformative technology of our times.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.000
From precision agriculture to precision medicine, from personalized e-commerce to personalized education.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:18.100
And from connected cars to connected homes, it's likely you're already experiencing many of the everyday applications of AI in your life.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.900
In this video series, you'll learn how AI works and why it matters.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:31.300
You'll see how with AI we can use data to train computers on just about anything.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:39.700
You'll explore how we can use AI to simulate neural networks in order to learn and how AEI enables computers to recognize objects too.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:47.200
And importantly, you learn about the broad societal impacts of AI and how to guard against unintended consequences.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:55.400
It's inspiring to see what AI can do in the hands of change makers who harness it to address societies.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.700
most pressing challenges. At the same time, we must ensure we build AI responsibly.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:06.800
taking a principled approach and asking the difficult questions like not what computers can do.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.500
but what computers should do. I'm excited to see what each of you will dream and invent with AI.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.800
and how you will apply this powerful technology to build the world that we all want to live in.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:21.800
I hope you enjoyed this course, thank you all very much.
